#. Tag: title
#: desktop.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "The desktop"
msgstr "The desktop"

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I add an application to the desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just choose the desired application from the <guimenu>K</guimenu> "
"menu and drag and drop it to the Desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For applications not listed in the <guimenu>K</guimenu> "
"menu, use the &RMB; on the desktop and choose <menuchoice><guimenuitem>"
"Create New</guimenuitem><guisubmenu>File</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Link to Application...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and fill in the configuration "
"for the application you want to link to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I mount/unmount a device from the desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, make sure you are allowed to <command>mount</command>/<command>"
"umount</command> the relevant device as a user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then you can add any device via &RMB; on the desktop and then choosing "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Create New</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Link to Device</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and then selecting the device of the "
"type you wish to control from the desktop. Fill in the settings for the device "
"in the dialog that appears and click <guilabel>OK</guilabel>"
". You can use the resulting desktop icon to mount/unmount the device from the "
"desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where are the icons kept?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The icons can be found only in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"KDEDIRS</envar>/share/icons</filename> or <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"HOME</envar>/.kde/share/icons</filename> or <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde2/share/icons</filename>. To use icons stored in other "
"locations, you must either copy them into one of the above-mentioned fixed "
"&kde; locations or make symlinks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I use the mouse scroll wheel in &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mouse wheel support comes with &Qt; 2.0 and above, so &kde; based on that will "
"automatically support the use of the mouse scroll wheel if your system is "
"configured correctly. Check your &X-Server; settings support the use of a "
"scrollwheel if it is not working."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I launch applications in a particular desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; comes with a program called &kstart;. To start an <application>"
"xterm</application> on the second desktop and then activate it use: <userinput>"
"<command>kstart</command> <option>--desktop 2 --activate --window \"xterm\" "
"</option>xterm</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that the <option>--window</option> option is important. It takes an "
"argument which is a regular expression matching the title of the window to "
"apply the settings to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please read <command>kstart</command> <option>--help-all</option> "
"for more magic available with &kstart; (and there is an abundance)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I save my files if I want them to appear directly on the desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/Desktop</filename>"
". You might need to refresh your desktop after you have saved your files."
msgstr ""

